DOCKER + CI/CD + DEPLOYMENT GUIDE

=====================================
FULL FLOW
=========

React → Docker → Docker Hub → Bitbucket → CI/CD → Render → Live URL

=====================================
PHASE 1: CREATE REACT APP (VITE)
================================

npm create vite@latest my-test-app
cd my-test-app
npm install
npm run dev

=====================================
PHASE 2: BUILD APP
==================

npm run build

Output:
dist/

=====================================
PHASE 3: DOCKER SETUP
=====================

Create Dockerfile:

FROM node:20-alpine AS build
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm install
COPY . .
RUN npm run build

FROM nginx:alpine
COPY --from=build /app/dist /usr/share/nginx/html

EXPOSE 80

CMD ["nginx", "-g", "daemon off;"]

---

Create .dockerignore:

node_modules
dist
.git

=====================================
PHASE 4: RUN DOCKER LOCALLY
===========================

docker build -t my-test-app .
docker run -p 8080:80 my-test-app

Open:
http://localhost:8080

=====================================
PHASE 5: PUSH TO DOCKER HUB
===========================

docker login
docker tag my-test-app ajithbharathi/my-test-app
docker push ajithbharathi/my-test-app

=====================================
PHASE 6: PUSH CODE TO BITBUCKET
===============================

git init
git add .
git commit -m "initial commit"

git remote add origin https://ajithbharathi@bitbucket.org/ajithbharathi/my-test-app.git

git push https://ajithbharathi:<TOKEN>@bitbucket.org/ajithbharathi/my-test-app.git

---

If error:
git pull origin main --rebase
git push origin main
--------------------

=====================================
PHASE 7: BITBUCKET PIPELINE (CI/CD)
===================================

Create file:
bitbucket-pipelines.yml

---

image: atlassian/default-image:3

pipelines:
branches:
main:
- step:
name: Build & Push Docker Image
services:
- docker
script:
- docker build -t ajithbharathi/my-test-app .
- echo $DOCKER_PASSWORD | docker login -u $DOCKER_USERNAME --password-stdin
- docker push ajithbharathi/my-test-app

---

Add variables in Bitbucket:

DOCKER_USERNAME = ajithbharathi
DOCKER_PASSWORD = <docker access token>

---

Trigger pipeline:
git add .
git commit -m "add pipeline"
git push

=====================================
PHASE 8: DEPLOY ON RENDER
=========================

Steps:

1. Go to Render
2. New → Web Service
3. Select "Existing Image"
4. Enter:
   ajithbharathi/my-test-app
5. Fill:
   Name: my-test-app
   Region: Singapore
   Instance: Free
6. Click "Create Web Service"

---

Output:
https://my-test-app.onrender.com

=====================================
PHASE 9: UPDATE FLOW
====================

git add .
git commit -m "update"
git push

Then:
Render → Manual Deploy → Deploy latest image

